    <!-- The sort chip's whole label. `library-browsing`: an ordering "reads as an ordering
         rather than as a value — a reader seeing the field name alone cannot tell a sort
         from a filter". The chip used to draw the bare field name, so beside a chip reading
         *Filter* it read as one of its values. The seven field names below are reused
         verbatim rather than respelt as sentences: a second wording of *Size on this device*
         in one app is how a vocabulary comes apart, and a capital after the colon is correct
         in all four languages where "Sorted by Size on this device" would not be. -->
